{
  "case_id": "2006-05-1256",
  "document_hash": "993aa0c4ef6b77e24ec87cc1352c15fd9435a9b5b0e61587f26188cb0fb7d929",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1256",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "993aa0c4ef6b77e24ec87cc1352c15fd9435a9b5b0e61587f26188cb0fb7d929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-993aa0c4ef6b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FREY: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: This case is here following this Court's remand to the Oregon courts to reconsider their decision in light of State Farm, a task at which we submit the Oregon courts completely failed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1256",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "993aa0c4ef6b77e24ec87cc1352c15fd9435a9b5b0e61587f26188cb0fb7d929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-993aa0c4ef6b-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Frey, are you talking about what is numbered, is it number 34?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1256",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "993aa0c4ef6b77e24ec87cc1352c15fd9435a9b5b0e61587f26188cb0fb7d929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-993aa0c4ef6b-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Isn't that the problem? If the instruction had said that, you would have a very different instruction, and I'm bothered by the instruction too for just that reason."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1256",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "993aa0c4ef6b77e24ec87cc1352c15fd9435a9b5b0e61587f26188cb0fb7d929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-993aa0c4ef6b-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FREY: Well, the second part of it is, what punishment means is what would be done in a class action, for instance, to impose punishment for all the harm suffered by Oregon smokers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Frey",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1256",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "993aa0c4ef6b77e24ec87cc1352c15fd9435a9b5b0e61587f26188cb0fb7d929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-993aa0c4ef6b-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What you're doing is preempting, you're allowing a potentially aberrational verdict, which there could be in many cases, to preempt the work of other juries."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1256",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "993aa0c4ef6b77e24ec87cc1352c15fd9435a9b5b0e61587f26188cb0fb7d929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-993aa0c4ef6b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You're losing me, counsel. What, what specifically is wrong with the instruction proposed here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Robert S. Peck",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1256",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "993aa0c4ef6b77e24ec87cc1352c15fd9435a9b5b0e61587f26188cb0fb7d929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-993aa0c4ef6b-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This instruction basically advises the jury to do precisely what Philip Morris argues before this Court it cannot do and that is to take into account the harm suffered by others in determining this disparity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1256",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "993aa0c4ef6b77e24ec87cc1352c15fd9435a9b5b0e61587f26188cb0fb7d929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-993aa0c4ef6b-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "60 percent of an award by statute goes to a crime victims fund of the State of Oregon and as soon as the judgment is rendered then the State becomes a judgment creditor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. PECK",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1256",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "993aa0c4ef6b77e24ec87cc1352c15fd9435a9b5b0e61587f26188cb0fb7d929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-993aa0c4ef6b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, you have to consider whether there is a likelihood that serious harm would arise from the defendant's misconduct. Second, the degree of the defendant's awareness of that likelihood. Three, profitability in the State of Oregon. Four, duration of the misconduct and concealment of it. Five, the attitude and the conduct of the defendant upon discovery of the misconduct. And then finally, financial condition of the defendant, which cuts both ways."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1256",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "993aa0c4ef6b77e24ec87cc1352c15fd9435a9b5b0e61587f26188cb0fb7d929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-993aa0c4ef6b-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The trouble with the more basic question, I don't know if you can answer it, but it is a problem, that when I -- most States have factors like that, or many do."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1256",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "993aa0c4ef6b77e24ec87cc1352c15fd9435a9b5b0e61587f26188cb0fb7d929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-993aa0c4ef6b-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I ask this question? Assuming there's a distinction, and the instruction does, between taking into account the extent of harm to others on the one hand and punishing for the extent of harm on the other."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1256",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "993aa0c4ef6b77e24ec87cc1352c15fd9435a9b5b0e61587f26188cb0fb7d929",
      "evidence_id": "ev-993aa0c4ef6b-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you think juries can, Oregon juries or juries anywhere can understand what they are told if they are told, you can take into account conduct directed at other people for the purpose of assessing how reprehensible the conduct is, but you can't punish for the harm that is caused other people?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1256",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "993aa0c4ef6b77e24ec87cc1352c15fd9435a9b5b0e61587f26188cb0fb7d929",
